# I9 — Execution-tier parity (hard)

Semantics for Core/runtime live **only** in `crates/jet-codegen/src/Prelude/**`.
AOT emit, Cranelift hosts, and interpreter ambient are **marshalling adapters**:
call the same Prelude `jet_*` / `*_defaulted` symbol AOT uses. Do not re-encode
policy, defaults, validation, or error maps in an engine.

Forbidden without an owner-ratified I9 carve-out that names a tier that cannot apply:

- Closing a feature AOT-only or with “JIT/interpreter later”
- Adding or keeping a durable `tests/jit_gaps.txt` / corpus exclusion for the change
- Parallel HTTP/net/Core logic in JIT hosts or ambient that does not call Prelude

Before claiming done: prove default `jet run` and AOT (`jet run --release`) against
the example golden when runnable. Reviewers reject I9 drift (see AGENTS.md I9,
architecture R12, `.claude/skills/verify/SKILL.md`).
